Duranium USB debug layer (duranium-usb-debug)
=============================================

What it is
----------
A development-only debug layer for postmarketOS Duranium, modelled on the
SM-T570 mainline bring-up console (gtactive3-mainline initramfs/init.c). It
brings up a USB NCM network interface and exposes, over that interface only:

  * root shell on TCP 2323      -> busybox "telnetd -l /bin/sh" (root, no auth)
  * register console on TCP 23 -> gta3-console from the device package, the
    same console as the bring-up init (scripts/tab, tab-get, tab-put)
  * adb (duranium-usb-debug-adb) -> adbd on FunctionFS: adb shell/push/pull
  * ssh on TCP 22             -> a dedicated sshd (its own host key)
  * kernel log on TCP 24      -> "dmesg -w", or /dev/kmsg without util-linux

Fixed addressing (matches the bring-up console so the host tooling in
gtactive3-mainline/scripts works unchanged):

  * gadget VID:PID 0x1d6b:0x0104
  * device MAC 02:57:0a:00:00:01  -> device link-local  fe80::57:aff:fe00:1
  * host   MAC 02:57:0a:00:00:02  -> host link-local     fe80::57:aff:fe00:2

Host usage (replace usb0 with the host's cdc_ncm interface):

  nc  fe80::57:aff:fe00:1%usb0 23          # raw root shell (telnetd -l /bin/sh)
  nc  fe80::57:aff:fe00:1%usb0 24 | less   # kernel log
  ssh root@fe80::57:aff:fe00:1%usb0        # needs a root key or password first

All three are socket-activated (systemd .socket units with Accept=yes),
listening on the wildcard address but bound to the gadget interface with
SO_BINDTODEVICE (BindToDevice=usb0). That works before the link has carrier
and before IPv6 duplicate address detection finished, which binding the
link-local address directly does not.

It is present both in the mkosi initrd (interface, telnet console and kernel
log; -initramfs subpackage) and in the booted system (adds sshd, which needs
the real root). The gadget stays bound across switch-root.

SECURITY
--------
This is an UNAUTHENTICATED root shell and an SSH daemon that permits root
login, reachable by anyone who can attach to the USB port. It is for
development images only. It listens on the USB gadget interface only and the
firewall (60_duranium_usb_debug.nft) only opens 22/23/24 on usb*, but USB
access is physical root access regardless. Do not ship it in a release image.

How to disable it
-----------------
Booted system, whole layer off (the target's Also= list covers every unit):
    systemctl disable --now duranium-usb-debug.target
Permanently, so a preset cannot re-enable it:
    systemctl mask duranium-usb-debug.target duranium-usb-debug.service \
        duranium-debug-shell.socket duranium-debug-sshd.socket \
        duranium-debug-klog.socket
Just one piece, e.g. keep the interface but drop the shell:
    systemctl disable --now duranium-debug-shell.socket
The initrd's units come from presets baked into the UKI and cannot be
disabled at runtime; the kernel command line switch covers the initrd and the
booted system alike:
    duranium.usb_debug=0

Release images
--------------
This layer is a SEPARATE package. A release image is built without it (drop
duranium-usb-debug from the device package's depends), so no masking is
needed.
